@page "/docs/pos"
@layout SiteLayout

<PageTitle>POS mode — DigiPay</PageTitle>


<main class="flex-1 page-enter">
    <DocsLayout Current="/docs/pos" Toc="toc">
        <Extra>
            <div class="dp-docs-extra">
                <a href="/features" class="dp-docs-nav-link">← Features tour</a>
            </div>
        </Extra>
        <ChildContent>
            <article class="dp-docs-article">
                <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-dgb-500 mb-2">Point-of-sale guide</p>
                <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3 slide-up">DigiPay POS mode</h1>
                <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-8 slide-up-delay-1">
                    Turn any tablet, phone, or spare laptop into a countertop DigiByte terminal in under a minute.
                    Staff don't need a DigiPay account — they pair the device once, then tap amounts all day.
                    You (the owner) stay in full control from the dashboard.
                </p>

                @* ---------- 1. Overview ---------- *@
                <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">1. What is POS mode?</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">
                        POS mode is a merchant-owned device that creates DigiPay sessions on the fly. The customer sees a QR + amount;
                        your staff sees an amount pad. Payments flow straight to your wallet — DigiPay never holds funds.
                    </p>
                    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mt-4">
                        <div class="card p-4">
                            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dgb-500 mb-1">Non-custodial</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">DGB lands in your wallet instantly. DigiPay never touches the keys.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card p-4">
                            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dgb-500 mb-1">No staff login</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">Staff see the amount pad and today's shift totals. A tablet can't record refunds, change settings or see API keys, and only works for its own store.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card p-4">
                            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dgb-500 mb-1">Looks after itself</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">The tablet remembers its pairing across reboots, keeps watching payments through dropped connections, and reloads itself between sales after an update.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 2. Pair a tablet ---------- *@
                <section id="pair" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">2. Pair a tablet</h2>
                    <ol class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal pl-5 mb-4">
                        <li>In the dashboard, open <strong>POS tablets</strong> and, if you like, give the tablet a name (e.g. <em>Front counter</em>). The tablet is paired to the store selected in the dashboard.</li>
                        <li>Click <strong>Generate code</strong>. A 6-character code appears with a countdown. It's valid for 10 minutes, can be used once, and stays on screen if you open another section and come back.</li>
                        <li>On the tablet, browse to <code class="font-mono text-xs px-1 py-0.5 bg-white dark:bg-dgb-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800 rounded">pay.dgbwallet.app/pos</code>.</li>
                        <li>Type the code and press <strong>Pair this device</strong> (or Enter). The dashboard switches to <em>Tablet paired</em>, and the tablet remembers itself from then on, with no sign-in at opening time.</li>
                        <li>Add the page to the home screen. On Safari: <em>Share → Add to Home Screen</em>. On Chrome: <em>⋮ → Install app</em>. It launches full-screen like a native app.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <figure class="mb-5 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800 bg-white dark:bg-dgb-900 shadow-sm">
                        <img src="/img/features/dashboard-pos-pair.png?v=2026-11-26"
                             alt="Dashboard POS tab showing a generated pairing code and list of paired devices"
                             loading="lazy"
                             class="block w-full h-auto" />
                        <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800">
                            Dashboard — generate a one-time pairing code and manage paired devices.
                        </figcaption>
                    </figure>

                    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-5">
                        <figure class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800 bg-white dark:bg-dgb-900 shadow-sm">
                            <img src="/img/features/pos-pairing.png?v=2026-11-26"
                                 alt="POS tablet pairing screen with 6-character code input"
                                 loading="lazy"
                                 class="block w-full h-auto" />
                            <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800">
                                Tablet — enter the pairing code.
                            </figcaption>
                        </figure>
                        <figure class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800 bg-white dark:bg-dgb-900 shadow-sm">
                            <img src="/img/features/pos-pairing-apikey.png?v=2026-11-26"
                                 alt="POS tablet pairing screen with API key tab selected"
                                 loading="lazy"
                                 class="block w-full h-auto" />
                            <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800">
                                Alternative — pair with a raw API key (headless setups).
                            </figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    </div>

                    <div class="p-3 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-900/20 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800/50 rounded-xl text-sm text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-200">
                        <strong>Tip:</strong> run several counters on separate codes. Each tablet shows up in the dashboard with its name, when it was last used, and <strong>Re-pair</strong> and <strong>Unpair</strong> buttons.
                    </div>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 3. Take a payment ---------- *@
                <section id="take-payment" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">3. Take a payment</h2>
                    <figure class="mb-5 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800 bg-white dark:bg-dgb-900 shadow-sm">
                        <img src="/img/features/pos-kiosk.png?v=2026-11-26"
                             alt="POS kiosk with keypad, amount, tip presets, and Charge button"
                             loading="lazy"
                             class="block w-full h-auto" />
                        <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dgb-800">
                            The paired tablet — amount pad, tip presets, and live DGB conversion.
                        </figcaption>
                    </figure>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">On the paired tablet:</p>
                    <ol class="space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal pl-5 mb-4">
                        <li>Pick the till currency with the currency button (DGB or any of about 80 currencies, searchable by name or country; your last few stay at the top).</li>
                        <li>Tap the amount, or a quick amount if you've set some. Optionally pick a tip: no tip, 10, 15 or 20 %. The DGB equivalent and the live rate show under the amount.</li>
                        <li>Tap <strong>Charge</strong>. The tablet creates the payment and shows the amount due and a QR code, with the DGB amount fixed at the current rate.</li>
                        <li>The customer scans with any DigiByte wallet (or taps <em>Open in wallet</em> on their phone).</li>
                        <li>Once the payment is detected the QR code is replaced by the confirmation progress (6 blocks, about 90 seconds). When it's confirmed the result screen shows and the till returns to the keypad after 5 seconds. <strong>Charge again</strong> keeps the amount if a sale expired or was underpaid.</li>
                        <li>Need to stop? <strong>Cancel sale</strong> cancels the payment on the server, so it can't be paid afterwards. It asks first if a payment has already been detected, and disappears once the customer has paid.</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Sales from a tablet are tagged with a <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-500 text-[10px] font-bold">POS</span> tag in the dashboard's <em>Payments</em> list.</p>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 4. Refund / void ---------- *@
                <section id="refund-void" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">4. Refund or void</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">
                        Crypto is not automatically reversible. Refunds happen off-platform — you send DGB back from your wallet and stamp the transaction ID into DigiPay so your records match.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Refund</strong> — only available for <em>Paid</em> or <em>Confirmed</em> sessions. Open the session in the dashboard, paste the refund txid + reason, and the session flips to <span class="inline-flex px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-500 text-[11px] font-semibold">Refunded</span>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Void</strong> — only for <em>Pending</em> or <em>Seen</em> sessions. Collapses the expiry so the chain watcher stops polling. Session becomes <span class="inline-flex px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-slate-500/15 text-slate-500 text-[11px] font-semibold">Voided</span>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Webhooks fire.</strong> <code class="font-mono text-xs">session.refunded</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs">session.voided</code> events POST to your store's webhook URL.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 5. Shift close ---------- *@
                <section id="shift-close" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">5. End-of-day close</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">
                        On the tablet, open the menu (top right) and choose <strong>Close shift</strong>. It shows the shift so far:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Collected</strong>: the DGB received, and the totals in each currency you charged in</li>
                        <li><strong>Tips</strong></li>
                        <li><strong>Outcomes</strong>: how many sales were paid, expired, underpaid or cancelled</li>
                        <li><strong>Missed revenue</strong>: what expired or underpaid sales were worth</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">The owner sees longer ranges in the dashboard's <em>Analytics</em> (7 / 30 / 90 / 365 days).</p>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 6. Audit trail ---------- *@
                <section id="audit" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">6. Audit trail</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">
                        Account changes (stores, API keys, webhooks, refunds and cancellations from the dashboard) are written to an append-only audit log,
                        with who made the change (the key's prefix, never the secret) and a short description.
                    </p>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Open the dashboard's <strong>Audit log</strong> to browse history. Sales from a tablet appear under <em>Payments</em> with a <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-500 text-[10px] font-bold">POS</span> tag and the tablet's name.</p>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 7. Manage devices ---------- *@
                <section id="manage-devices" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">7. Manage devices</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">The dashboard's <em>POS tablets</em> section lists every paired tablet:</p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Name and store</strong>: what you called it, and the store it takes payments for.</li>
                        <li><strong>Last used</strong>: the last time the tablet did anything.</li>
                        <li><strong>Re-pair</strong>: makes a new code for that tablet (for a reset or a new device). Once the new pairing goes through, the old key stops working.</li>
                        <li><strong>Unpair</strong>: revokes the tablet's key straight away. The tablet goes back to the pairing screen on its next sale.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">If a tablet is lost or stolen, <strong>Unpair</strong> it. A tablet paired before tablets were tied to one store is marked in the list; re-pair it to limit it to its store.</p>
                </section>

                @* ---------- 8. Tablet settings ---------- *@
                <section id="settings" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">8. Tablet settings</h2>
                    <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3">Menu → <strong>Tablet settings</strong>, saved on each tablet:</p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Layout</strong>: Auto (side by side on a wide landscape screen, stacked otherwise), Split, Stacked, or Compact for small phones.</li>
                        <li><strong>Keypad</strong>: phone order (1-2-3 on top) or calculator order (7-8-9 on top), and which side the keypad sits on in Split.</li>
                        <li><strong>Customer display</strong>: Standard, or Full-screen QR so the customer sees just the amount and the code.</li>
                        <li><strong>Quick amounts</strong>: up to 6 preset amounts per currency. Optional <strong>00 key</strong> and a vibration on each key press.</li>
                        <li><strong>Theme</strong>: Dark, Light or match the device.</li>
                        <li><strong>Manager PIN</strong>: a 4–8 digit PIN that's asked before the tablet can be unpaired. Changing or removing it asks for the current PIN.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                @* ---------- FAQ ---------- *@
                <section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">FAQ</h2>
                    <div class="space-y-4">
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Do I need a separate hardware terminal?</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">No. Any browser-capable device works — iPad, Android tablet, cheap Windows tablet, Chromebook, even a phone.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">What happens if the internet drops mid-sale?</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">The tablet can't create a new session without the API, but in-flight sessions continue — the customer's wallet still broadcasts to the chain, and DigiPay reconciles when you come back online. An offline queue is on the roadmap.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Can staff see the store's revenue or refund sessions?</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">No. The POS token only permits creating sessions and reading the session it just created. Refunds and revoke actions require the dashboard (which needs the owner's Digi-ID).</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Can I run POS on a customer's phone?</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">Don't. POS devices hold a long-lived session token. Pair only devices your business owns.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Does it support multiple currencies?</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">Yes. The till can charge in DGB or in any of about 80 currencies, the same list as the DigiByte wallet. The DGB amount is worked out at the live rate (directly where CoinGecko quotes DGB in that currency, otherwise through the USD rate) and fixed when the sale is created.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                @* ---------- CTA ---------- *@
                <section class="mt-12 p-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-dgb-500/10 to-dgb-500/5 border border-dgb-500/20 rounded-2xl text-center">
                    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Ready to go live?</h2>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4 m-0">Pair your first tablet from the dashboard's POS tab.</p>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center">
                        <a href="/merchant" class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">Open dashboard</a>
                        <a href="/features" class="card inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 no-underline text-sm font-semibold transition-colors">See all features</a>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </article>
        </ChildContent>
    </DocsLayout>
</main>

